  ('3cc1b8a6-ed07-5418-86c7-f24256bf1cc3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Based on paragraph 4, what can the reader infer about scientists' understanding of octopus camouflage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They believe octopuses do not really match their surroundings at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They still do not fully know how octopuses match colors they may not see.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They have proven that the skin senses light and controls every color.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"They have shown that octopuses see colors more clearly than people.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They still do not fully know how octopuses match colors they may not see.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 gives two possible explanations and says, "The question has not been settled." The skin idea is only what "some researchers think," so calling it proven goes beyond the text.$q$, 'draft', 'fdd8d2ba-d0d3-5ea0-af25-191be06d1a27')
