   $q$In paragraph 4, the author writes, "Then the wind changed its mind." What does this phrase mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The judges changed the rules of the kite contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The wind decided to stop blowing for the rest of the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-extreme"},{"text":"The wind suddenly shifted in a different direction or strength.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Tomasz decided he no longer wanted to fly his kite.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-characters"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The wind suddenly shifted in a different direction or strength.$q$, $q$Right after this phrase, the kite "dipped and spun," which shows the wind suddenly changed how it was blowing. The wind did not stop completely, because the kite steadied itself and kept flying.$q$, 'draft', '781cc872-cb16-529e-bd69-22390ad00008')
