values
  ('afa454d8-e960-5532-a0bc-686fdbf3c301', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In the last paragraph, Tomasz feels "as if the sky had shaken hands with him." What does this personification suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tomasz was disappointed that the sky had blown his kite away at the end of the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Tomasz's hands were sore because the string had cut into his fingers all day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Flying the kite made him feel a friendly connection with the sky that he would remember.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The judges came over and shook Tomasz's hand to congratulate him on his prize.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-characters"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Flying the kite made him feel a friendly connection with the sky that he would remember.$q$, $q$A handshake is a friendly greeting, and Tomasz still feels "the pull of the string," so the sky is treated like a new friend he connected with. The kite was never lost, and the judges are not described shaking hands.$q$, 'draft', '781cc872-cb16-529e-bd69-22390ad00008')
