   $q$In paragraph 5, Grandma Ines says, "Rome was not built in a day." What does she mean by this saying?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lucia should learn about the history of Rome before she sews.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The cape must be finished today or it will not be ready.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Lucia should quit because sewing is too hard for her age.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Learning a new skill takes time, so Lucia should keep practicing.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Learning a new skill takes time, so Lucia should keep practicing.$q$, $q$Grandma says this when Lucia wants to quit, and adds "Neither is a cape," meaning good work takes time. She encourages Lucia, so the saying does not mean Lucia should give up.$q$, 'draft', '338e4de6-03eb-59ed-98b0-cf3e3bb871b0')
