   $q$In paragraph 5, the owner "greets it like a returning hero." What does this simile suggest about the owner's feelings?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The owner is surprised, because the pigeon was not expected to return home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The owner believes the pigeon rescued someone during its long flight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The owner is upset, because the pigeon took too long to finish its flight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The owner is proud and grateful that the pigeon finished such a hard journey.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The owner is proud and grateful that the pigeon finished such a hard journey.$q$, $q$People welcome heroes with pride and thanks after a difficult task, and the pigeon has just finished "a long flight." Homing pigeons are expected to return, so surprise does not fit the text.$q$, 'draft', '1f1ed3c4-411a-5394-b541-ca3671e3ad70')
