   $q$In paragraph 1, the author writes that "the owl's workday begins" when the sun goes down. What does "workday" mean here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"the time when the owl starts hunting for food","is_correct":true},{"text":"the hours when the owl teaches young birds","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"the job the owl does for farmers who pay it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"the time when the owl goes to sleep in its nest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$the time when the owl starts hunting for food$q$, $q$The next sentences explain that owls are "active at night" and built "for finding food," so the owl's work is hunting. Owls rest during the day, not at sundown.$q$, 'draft', '21993381-eb45-59f2-a452-331fee5c2025')
