   $q$How does calling the kite "a stubborn spark" in the last stanza help develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the speaker is annoyed that the kite will not come back down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It links the kite to the speaker's refusal to quit, showing that persistence pays off.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests the kite is dangerous and could start a fire on the dry hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It reveals that the brother was the one who wanted to keep trying all along.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It links the kite to the speaker's refusal to quit, showing that persistence pays off.$q$, $q$The speaker was stubborn by saying "One more" when the brother wanted to leave, so calling the kite stubborn connects its success to that persistence. The word "spark" describes the bright red color, not a real fire.$q$, 'draft', 'c78c6fb3-fe3c-54c4-af48-4e9107ad198a')
