   $q$Why does the author include the paragraph in which Pip laughs at Bramble?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It describes the weather that makes the winter come so early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-paragraph"},{"text":"It explains how Bramble learned to scratch marks into the bark.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Pip is the wiser squirrel and will win in the end.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"It sets up a prediction that the winter events will prove wrong.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sets up a prediction that the winter events will prove wrong.$q$, $q$Pip predicts that Bramble "will go hungry by the first snow," and the winter section shows the opposite: Pip is the one who goes hungry. The paragraph builds the contrast that the ending reverses, rather than showing Pip as wise.$q$, 'draft', 'c00c3fb3-de69-51d1-b977-2a36f9ee17e4')
