   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bats cannot see at all, so they must make loud calls that people hear at night. The calls scare insects out of trees so the bats can catch them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Scientists record bat calls at night. Just before a bat catches a moth, its calls speed up into a rapid buzz that people can hear on the recordings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Bats send out high calls and listen for the echoes. The echoes tell them where objects are, so they can fly safely and catch insects in the dark.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Bats are the most amazing animals on Earth. Everyone should protect them because their hunting skills are better than anything people have invented.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bats send out high calls and listen for the echoes. The echoes tell them where objects are, so they can fly safely and catch insects in the dark.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "Bats send out high calls" covers how echolocation works and what it lets bats do, without adding opinions. The choice calling bats "the most amazing animals on Earth" adds the summarizer's own judgments, such as "most amazing," which do not belong in an objective summary.$q$, 'draft', 'bb205585-475f-5ebb-90b5-07e4782823a2')
