   $q$What is the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Food kept cold with lake ice tasted better than food kept in refrigerators.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Workers used long saws to cut frozen lakes into a grid of large blocks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Many old jobs have disappeared over time because of new inventions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Harvesting lake ice was once an important way to keep food cold, until machines replaced it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Harvesting lake ice was once an important way to keep food cold, until machines replaced it.$q$, $q$The passage explains how ice was cut, stored and delivered to keep food cold, and then how machines ended the business. The sawing detail is only one step described in paragraph 2.$q$, 'draft', '23ca879d-994d-53e3-9bbc-185f2367c374')
