   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ice harvesting was cold, hard work that no one should have had to do. Refrigerators were the greatest invention of the 1900s because they ended it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"In the 1800s, workers cut ice from frozen lakes, stored it in insulated icehouses and delivered it in summer to keep food cold. Machines and refrigerators later ended the business.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Families made ice in their own iceboxes during winter and saved it for summer. Later, factories began selling refrigerators, so the iceboxes were thrown away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Crews cleared snow from frozen lakes and marked the ice into a grid. Then workers cut blocks with saws and floated them through channels to shore.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In the 1800s, workers cut ice from frozen lakes, stored it in insulated icehouses and delivered it in summer to keep food cold. Machines and refrigerators later ended the business.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "In the 1800s, workers cut ice" covers cutting, storing, delivering and the end of the business in neutral words. The choice saying families made ice in their own iceboxes sounds complete but is wrong, because workers cut ice from lakes, not inside family iceboxes.$q$, 'draft', '23ca879d-994d-53e3-9bbc-185f2367c374')
