   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Paper is sorted by type and then mixed with water in a big tank called a pulper. Screens take out staples and tape from the pulp.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Recycled paper is sorted, made into pulp, cleaned of trash and ink, then pressed into new sheets. Its fibers weaken each time, so it can be recycled only several times.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Paper is sorted, turned into pulp, cleaned and pressed into new sheets. Because the fibers never wear out, the same paper can be recycled again and again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Recycling paper is the most important chore a family can do. People who throw paper in the trash are not doing their part to save the forests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Recycled paper is sorted, made into pulp, cleaned of trash and ink, then pressed into new sheets. Its fibers weaken each time, so it can be recycled only several times.$q$, $q$The choice ending "it can be recycled only several times" covers every major step and the limit on recycling in neutral words. The choice saying the same paper can be recycled again and again looks complete but says fibers never wear out, which paragraph 6 contradicts.$q$, 'draft', '3079d50c-92ae-53ec-8cf2-a5d6b8c5bb75')
