   $q$According to the passage, why did Amara need her kite to be flying at noon?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The small boy wanted to watch the heron during lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The wind at Harbor Park always died down after noon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The judges would only score kites that were in the air.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Her grandfather had to leave the festival soon after noon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The judges would only score kites that were in the air.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says the judging began at noon and "the judges only scored kites that were in the air." Nothing in the text mentions the wind changing at noon.$q$, 'draft', '715d8257-deb1-5d23-8b8b-a0474ce58853')
