   $q$Why does the speaker say Mr. Delgado's "Same time next week?" may not really be a question?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Delgado is giving an order that the speaker must follow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The speaker rides every Saturday, so both already know the answer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mr. Delgado speaks so softly that the speaker cannot hear him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker plans to stop riding the bus after this Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker rides every Saturday, so both already know the answer.$q$, $q$The driver "knows my name," and the poem shows a weekly routine, so "same time next week" is a friendly certainty rather than a real question. The speaker says yes, so there is no sign of quitting the bus.$q$, 'draft', '097c5756-49d9-52c5-b267-898e73526c9c')
