   $q$Which detail best shows the theme developing in the middle of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mateo copies the red lines from the old map into his notebook.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Mrs. Abernathy unrolls a yellowed map on a glass table at the museum.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"setting-not-development"},{"text":"Mateo realizes the \"Car Barn\" he passed for years once held trolleys.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Each student has to find something older than their grandparents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"background-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mateo realizes the "Car Barn" he passed for years once held trolleys.$q$, $q$The "Car Barn" detail shows a familiar building suddenly meaning something new to Mateo, which is the theme at work. The assignment is background that starts the plot, but it does not show his view of the town changing.$q$, 'draft', '14fcc73f-3c0a-5788-a24e-329e490e74c3')
