   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A good teacher will fix every mistake a student makes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Skill grows through patient practice, even after many failures.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Cups and bowls are more useful when they are made by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Making pottery is too difficult for most beginners to learn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Skill grows through patient practice, even after many failures.$q$, $q$The speaker fails three times, keeps trying and ends with seven cups. The poem does not say pottery is too hard, because the speaker does learn it.$q$, 'draft', '179ba9a1-e7d8-5901-ae6b-a2ff5d8f8340')
