   $q$The Latin root port means "carry," and the suffix -able means "able to be." What is a "portable scoreboard"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A scoreboard that keeps score without any help","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A scoreboard that can be carried from place to place","is_correct":true},{"text":"A scoreboard that shows the scores very brightly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A scoreboard that is attached to a wall for good","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A scoreboard that can be carried from place to place$q$, $q$Portable means "able to be carried," and the passage says a volunteer carried it to the finish line. A scoreboard fixed to a wall is the opposite of portable.$q$, 'draft', '1062a784-bfcb-5328-ba64-5da8d5c830ef')
