   $q$The prefix in- can mean "into," and spect means "look." What did the coach want Keoni to do when he asked him to "inspect each baton"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Carry each baton to the starting line for runners","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"Wrap each baton with fresh tape before the race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Count the batons to be sure none were missing","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Look closely at each baton to check for problems","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Look closely at each baton to check for problems$q$, $q$To inspect is to "look into" something carefully, and Keoni turned each baton in his hands looking for cracks or loose tape. He checked the tape, but the passage never says he wrapped new tape on the batons.$q$, 'draft', '1062a784-bfcb-5328-ba64-5da8d5c830ef')
