   $q$The prefix e- means "out," and the Latin root rupt means "break." What happened when the crowd's noise began to "erupt"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The noise burst out suddenly and loudly","is_correct":true},{"text":"The noise stayed at the same steady level","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"The noise broke the scoreboard on the table","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The noise slowly faded until it stopped","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The noise burst out suddenly and loudly$q$, $q$Erupt means "break out," so the crowd's cheering suddenly burst out as another runner caught up. The noise did not literally break anything; the root describes how sudden and strong the sound was.$q$, 'draft', '1062a784-bfcb-5328-ba64-5da8d5c830ef')
