   $q$The prefix pre- means "before," and the Latin root serv means "keep" or "save." What do the museum workers' steps help do when they "preserve images"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Copy the images onto new and brighter plates","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Prepare the images before they are first taken","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal-prefix"},{"text":"Serve the images to visitors who ask to see them","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"Keep the images safe so they last a long time","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keep the images safe so they last a long time$q$, $q$Preserve means to keep something safe ahead of time, and the gloves, low light, and cool rooms all protect the old pictures. The word "serve" looks similar, but serv here means "keep," not "hand out."$q$, 'draft', '337bd9ff-2f1a-578c-8da0-3ceca4af637e')
