   $q$The word "visit" shares the root vis, meaning "see," with "invisible." Based on this root, why does the narrator say the video call was "the closest thing to a visit"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A visit means living with someone, and the call lets them share a home","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"A visit means calling someone, and the call uses a telephone line","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"circular-reasoning"},{"text":"A visit means writing to someone, and the call lets them send letters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"A visit means going to see someone, and the call lets them see each other","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A visit means going to see someone, and the call lets them see each other$q$, $q$Vis means "see," so a visit is going to see someone, and the video call lets Priya and Grandma see each other even though they are far apart. Writing letters has nothing to do with the root vis.$q$, 'draft', 'b30167b8-e836-5642-a884-a4c4479be157')
