  ('fe6f6504-a2ba-5537-b868-89fe7fffa819', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The prefix pre- means "before," and the Latin root dict means "say." What did Mateo ask Ms. Adeyemi to do when he asked her to "predict" how students would feel?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ask students how they felt about the salad bar","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker"},{"text":"Say what she thought would happen before it happened","is_correct":true},{"text":"Explain what students had already said about it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-tense"},{"text":"Write down a list of foods for the salad bar","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Say what she thought would happen before it happened$q$, $q$Predict means "say before," and Ms. Adeyemi guessed ahead of time that the cucumbers would disappear first. The salad bar was new, so she was not reporting what students had already said.$q$, 'draft', '598c7be7-aa40-5381-a913-87a5d9bd836c')
