   $q$The prefix bi- means "two," and the Greek root cycl means "circle" or "wheel." What is a "bicycle"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A vehicle with one wheel","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-prefix-meaning"},{"text":"A vehicle with two wheels","is_correct":true},{"text":"A vehicle pulled by a horse","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A vehicle with a motor","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A vehicle with two wheels$q$, $q$Bi means "two" and cycl means "wheel," so a bicycle has two wheels, like the safety bicycle with two wheels of equal size. A vehicle with one wheel is a unicycle.$q$, 'draft', '98c91e10-4d4f-529e-8c24-b36cde61f489')
