  ('4cbff809-3843-59c7-b762-04f75d140c30', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The prefix in- can mean "upon," the Latin root vent means "come," and the suffix -or means "one who." Who were the "inventors" who added pedals?$q$, $q$[{"text":"People who came up with new ideas and devices","is_correct":true},{"text":"People who rode bicycles on long trips","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"People who sold bicycles in their stores","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"People who came to watch bicycle races","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$People who came up with new ideas and devices$q$, $q$An inventor is "one who comes upon" something new, and these people added pedals that the first bicycles did not have. Coming to watch races uses the meaning "come" too literally and ignores what the inventors actually did.$q$, 'draft', '98c91e10-4d4f-529e-8c24-b36cde61f489')
