   $q$The prefix ab- can mean "off," and the Latin root rupt means "break." What does it mean that the music stopped "abruptly"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It stopped slowly as the song came to an end","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It stopped because someone broke a speaker","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It stopped on purpose for a quiet scene","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It stopped suddenly, without any warning","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It stopped suddenly, without any warning$q$, $q$Abruptly means "broken off," so the music cut off all at once when the sound board lost power. Nothing was physically broken; the root describes how sudden the stop was.$q$, 'draft', 'b61e01fc-665f-5c02-abc0-f08a9871079d')
