   $q$Why is Mr. Adeyemi's evidence weaker than the evidence from the university study?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is about science lessons instead of an article about volcanoes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"It comes from a middle school, so it cannot apply to any students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"It shows that self-quizzing made his students remember much less.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It is one teacher's impression, with no scores or comparison group.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is one teacher's impression, with no scores or comparison group.$q$, $q$He "says his students now seem to remember" more, which is an observation without measured results or a group to compare against. The study measured test scores for two matched groups.$q$, 'draft', '7b3d51ac-2729-566d-8092-73d5770ad2eb')
